// EMA pullback continuation. Nano computes both averages from a declared
// `close` input: EMA(close, 20) over EMA(close, 50) is the trend, and a close
// that has fallen back to the fast average while still holding the slow one is
// the pullback. Nothing here is host-derived except the price series itself.
// REGIME: an established uptrend that breathes. Do NOT fire in a downtrend or
// in a range - when the fast average sits under the slow one this rule is
// silent by construction, and in a range the two averages braid together so
// "pullback" and "breakdown" become the same bar.
// INPUTS: close (series<float>). No other host signal.
// CONDITIONS: fast EMA above slow EMA, and the close inside the band between
// them. Both halves are load-bearing - the trend test alone buys extension,
// the pullback test alone buys every decline.
// INVALIDATION: a close below the slow average. The pullback thesis assumes
// the slow average is support; once it is not, this is a failed trend, and the
// rule goes silent on its own because the second condition inverts.
// SHAPE: 1d; a stair-step advance that keeps returning to the 20-day line.
// NOT golden_cross: that fires once, on the crossing bar, and says the trend
// began. This fires repeatedly, inside a trend that already exists, and says
// nothing about when it started. NOT rsi_oversold_reversal: that measures
// exhaustion in an oscillator; this measures location against two averages and
// can fire with RSI at 55.
// CALIBRATED ON: liquid US equity index proxies, daily. 20/50 is a convention,
// not a discovery - the pair only needs to be far enough apart that the band
// between them is wide enough to catch a normal pullback. Both periods are
// `param`s so a host can re-fit them without editing the rule.
strategy EmaPullbackContinuation {

    param fast: int = 20
    param slow: int = 50

    input close: series<float>

    let fast_ma = EMA(close, fast)
    let slow_ma = EMA(close, slow)
    let uptrend = fast_ma > slow_ma
    let pullback = close <= fast_ma and close > slow_ma

    every 1d {

        if uptrend and pullback {

            buy(SPY, 0.65)

        }

    }

}
